# wagon: the flow of depot yardr's wagons. A wagon is one piece of a train, built
# in parallel with its siblings: the builder tests it with the depot's test
# command (.yardr/test: only what it changed and what imports that is
# tested), the assembly lands it on the train's branch after the same run,
# without YARDR_LANDING, and nobody reviews it by itself. The whole suite and
# the reviews, one of them for security alone, are the train's, on the whole,
# before main moves (yardr.train.flow). So there is no review stage here. A
# wagon with no train never leaves backlog: yardr refuses the move. See
# docs/line.md#wagons.
backlog -> new
new -> approved on done | decide on question | backlog
approved -> merged on done | new on failed | decide on question
decide -> backlog | new
merged terminal
